:"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization and locking on M, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fixed start vector; once k pairs are found, a run on the complement of their vectors checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that no copy of a multiple eigenvalue was missed. A Ritz pair is accepted when its residual"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · max(|λ|, s\/1000), s Gershgorin’s bound on the spectrum; the vectors"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, whose values are returned. The dense solver below 64"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, or when k is a third of them or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"0 is no edge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"largest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", every weight is finite","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and nonnegative, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when a Lanczos run spends ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" products without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"converging, with the products spent and the largest Ritz residual on the tolerance’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scale. The dense solver throws as ","type":"text"},{"code":"adjacencySpectrum","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/laplacianeigenpairs(largest:weight:tolerance:maxiterations:)-1nz26"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs.swift#L525","fileName":"Eigenpairs.swift"},"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpectralGraphTheory"}],"title":"laplacianEigenpairs(largest:weight:tolerance:maxIterations:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE19laplacianEigenpairs7largest6weight9tolerance13maxIterationsAD0F0VyxGSi_qd__5Edges_5IndexQZXESdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKSBRd__lF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"laplacianEigenpairs"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"largest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIde